  <!-- ===================== FAQ ===================== -->
  <section id="docs">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cmd-title reveal"><span class="pr">$</span> failora help <span class="arg">--faq</span></div>
      <div class="faq reveal">
        <details open>
          <summary>What does a URL scan check?</summary>
          <div class="ans">The planned URL scan will check whether the page responds, how long it takes, and common header and configuration settings. Only scan URLs you own or have permission to test.</div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How does a private repository connect?</summary>
          <div class="ans">Repository analysis is planned. The connection flow and access rules will be documented before launch.</div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How is recovery verification done?</summary>
          <div class="ans">Failora injects controlled failures such as timeouts, HTTP 429, HTTP 500 and malformed responses into your target. It then checks whether retries and fallbacks run, and records success rate and latency.</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

